      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2017 John Wiley & Sons A/S. Published by John Wiley & Sons Ltd.",
        "AbstractText": "This case describes a patient being considered for combined liver-kidney transplantation for Caroli's disease with a failed renal transplant. A chronic septic focus could not be located with standard imaging techniques, such as ultrasonography and computed tomography. This case report highlights the observation that a retained non-functioning transplant can be the cause of fever of unknown origin and PET-CT can be useful in diagnosing these challenging cases."
      },
